+- Disabled entirely `iAIHandicapIncrementTurns`, which would give per turn discounts to AI, making the game gradually harder as the game went on if i understood it correctly with chatgpt 5 too. This was especially aggressive at highest difficulties, and now that our AI is efficient with its hammer usage or more so at least but anyways etc, it would always run away being unbeatable even in emperor autoplay i assume/guess thanks to all the AI enhancements to hammer usage we made. I hope to provide a fair and challenging, winnable challenge not this mess, so disabled it entirely (set to 0 as of now as was in lower difficulties anyways etc). This means the handicap settings like unit hammer to produce reduction, or buildings, or research, etc if any more anyways etc, that were all affected by this, now are rather only influenced by the corresponding handicap xml fields rather (such as `iAITrainPercent` for unit hammer to produce for example anyways etc). I have adjusted these xml fields so game is hard but not in an exponential per turn, gradually impossible to overcome way and perhaps painful but anyways etc, but instead linear per handicap setting that are fair and hard as much as possible rather, to accomodate for this change too. We rely on our AI competency and efficiency improvements rather to provide the needed challenge i want in advciv-sas rather but anyways etc. I also believe it will help AI longterm, as by producing less untis since thye produce so much, they won't go bankrupt too soon if at all, which should help their economy long-term, especially to go from middle game to endgame, which would otherwise become way too warlike xd and lose the early tension of a close game now not possible to match for the human player due to AI just producing too much more units, hopefully more balanced, fun, and harder than base advciv in a fair way now instead, at least i tried to, but anwyays etc.
 
